  "runner_adaptations": [
    "Construct current particlegan.get_recipe explicitly; never use gan_v3_recipe or LegacyRecipe for RP2.",
    "Keep evaluation steps outside recipe; total_steps remains None. Existing host_recipe and native resolve_config write numeric total_steps and must get a distinct continuous route.",
    "Preserve each frozen task architecture/resource card, initialization order, data streams, fixed seed, evaluator samples, thresholds and observation times; do not replace all tasks with ring resources.",
    "Use trainer-owned fixed absolute noise bootstrap once. Existing toy100_compatibility and native train wrappers add external horizon-based noise and can double-noise current trainer.",
    "Bypass old cosine FixedControl, optimizer_defaults schedule patches and step_with_policy LR hooks; log actual precision scales/noise/controller state on every update.",
    "Carry and verify full Recipe.to_dict identity including continuous_precision and adam_eager_state. LegacyRecipe.to_dict and GLOBAL_RECIPE_FIELDS omit these fields.",
    "Version the candidate execution-receipt checks to support autonomous control while retaining unchanged live quality graders. Old common22 regrader explicitly expects horizon cosine/noise receipts.",
    "Snapshot all public package files plus any new runner/controller adapters and prove imported module locations. Native full-source and suite.snapshot utilities are reusable."
  ],
  "learner_api_gaps": [
    "ReversiblePrecision is instantiated and advanced only inside GANTrainer. Recipe.make_* factories provide KA2/eager Adam but do not apply RP2 scales or observe precision; factory-only loops silently omit RP2.",
    "GANTrainer handles unconditional scalar GANs with one exact ParticlePrior and no encoder; it cannot faithfully execute eight conditional/direct-particle/AE/multi-prior hosts unchanged.",
    "A public reusable component binding is needed for those eight: one consistent controller/critic reference per game, scales before paired D/G updates, normalized actual update activity, ordinary real-data gradient disagreement after update, fixed noise policy, checkpoint state. Conditional roles need data-coordinate differentiation without feeding labels/centers/evaluator scores to policy.",
    "Multiple prior tables require explicit A2 ownership rather than hiding them in a generic module and losing damping; direct sample particles need the public direct-response path.",
    "Current learning_rate_scales and scale_learning_rates do not accept None horizons or autonomous controller state; their use would fail or substitute an unrelated schedule."
  ],
  "misreporting_risks": [
    "public_default_verification verifies19 historical GAN-v3 tasks; its name and GANTrainer calls do not imply RP2 qualification.",
    "toy_suite --with-default-control adds an optional installed-wheel GAN-v3 control; its passes cannot fill missing RP2 cases.",
    "toy100_compatibility.declared_recipe selects old global fields then constructs gan_v3_recipe, dropping candidate controller identity.",
    "Historical LegacyRecipe.make_critic_optimizer explicitly returns K3PCriticAdam and bypasses new eager factory; blindly retaining this adapter can mix generator and critic formulations.",
    "Nine old custom hosts use ordinary Adam/global host patches; inherited labels do not establish public KA2 or precision execution.",
    "All19 require complete24-observation live evidence and frozen sustained gates. Each native requires coverage AND accuracy (five final evaluations plus independent fixed holdout). EMA/endpoints/ancestor passes cannot substitute.",
    "Unimplemented custom routes remain NOT_RUN. Do not rewrite their targets/losses into unconditional GANs merely to force GANTrainer coverage."
  ],
